# addon.xml Manifest Rules

## Required Root Attributes

The `<addon>` element must always have these four attributes:

```xml
<addon id="plugin.video.themoviedb.helper"
       version="6.15.1"
       name="TMDb Helper"
       provider-name="jurialmunkey">
```

- `id` -- must match the addon folder name exactly.
- `version` -- semantic versioning `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`. Bump on every release.
- `name` -- human-readable display name.
- `provider-name` -- author/developer name.

## Dependencies (`<requires>`)

```xml
<requires>
  <import addon="xbmc.python" version="3.0.1"/>
  <import addon="script.module.requests" version="2.9.1"/>
</requires>
```

- Always include `xbmc.python` with the minimum required version.
- Add `<import>` entries for every script module the addon depends on.
- Version numbers are **minimum** versions, not exact pins.
- Optional dependencies use `optional="true"`: `<import addon="..." version="..." optional="true"/>`.

## Extension Points

Each `<extension>` must have a `point` attribute and its `library` must point to an existing file:

| Point | Library | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `xbmc.python.pluginsource` | `resources/plugin.py` | Main video plugin |
| `xbmc.python.script` | `resources/script.py` | Script actions |
| `xbmc.service` | `resources/service.py` | Background service |
| `xbmc.python.module` | `resources/modules` | Shared module |
| `xbmc.addon.metadata` | (none) | Addon metadata |

- The pluginsource extension must include `<provides>video</provides>`.
- Do not remove or rename extension points without updating the corresponding Python files.

## Metadata Extension

```xml
<extension point="xbmc.addon.metadata">
  <reuselanguageinvoker>false</reuselanguageinvoker>
  <summary lang="en_GB">Short summary</summary>
  <description lang="en_GB">Longer description</description>
  <disclaimer lang="en_GB">Data attribution</disclaimer>
  <license>GPL-3.0-or-later</license>
  <website>https://github.com/...</website>
  <forum>https://forum.kodi.tv/...</forum>
  <assets>
    <icon>icon.png</icon>
    <fanart>fanart.jpg</fanart>
    <clearlogo>clearlogo.png</clearlogo>
    <screenshot>resources/screenshot-01.jpg</screenshot>
  </assets>
</extension>
```

- Every `<summary>`, `<description>`, and `<disclaimer>` must have a `lang` attribute.
- When adding a new locale, add entries for all three text elements.
- `<assets>` paths are relative to the addon root. Verify files exist before referencing them.
- `<reuselanguageinvoker>` is `false` for this addon -- do not change without understanding the implications (affects global state persistence between invocations).

## Checklist When Editing

1. Bump `version` if making a release-worthy change.
2. If adding a new Python dependency, add the corresponding `<import>` in `<requires>`.
3. If adding a new entry point file, add a matching `<extension>` element.
4. Keep multi-language metadata in sync across all existing locales.
5. Validate XML is well-formed before committing.
